  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What run_azure.sh does",
      "items": [
        "Run from Cloud Shell. Every step is idempotent: 1 pre-flight (tools, login, resource providers), 2 infra (resource group, Azure SQL, storage, ACR, AKS), 3 cluster (start a paused AKS, scale nodes, secrets, ACR pull access).",
        "4 database tables come from Flyway inside t24-mock-cbs, 5 az acr build for only the missing images (3 in parallel), 6 deploy dependencies then services, 7 self-heal by adding a node when a pod is Pending (up to MAX_NODES=4), 8 smoke test the gateway, login path and web apps."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Azure resources it creates or reuses",
      "items": [
        "Resource group (auto-detected, else rg-aurabank-<id> in southeastasia). Azure SQL server with sqldb-master at S1 and a 0.0.0.0 rule that allows Azure services. Storage account with a compliance-vault container. ACR Basic with admin enabled. AKS tries several VM sizes: Standard_B2s, D2s_v3, B2ms, D4s_v3, D2as_v5.",
        "Names for SQL, ACR and storage carry a suffix hashed from subscription and resource group so teammates sharing a subscription do not collide.",
        "banking-secrets holds the SQL, Postgres, storage, JWT and Datadog values; acr-secret is attached to the default service account."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Exposure to review",
      "items": [
        "Gateway, staff console and customer web each get a public LoadBalancer IP, and all traffic is plain HTTP. The mobile app is pointed at http://<gateway-ip>:8080.",
        "MailHog is public with no authentication by default (EXPOSE_MAILHOG=true), so anyone with the IP can read OTP emails. Set EXPOSE_MAILHOG=false for anything beyond testing.",
        "Redis, Postgres, Kafka and MailHog run as single in-cluster pods, not Azure PaaS. Gateway also routes to CBS and risk; services use Redis and Kafka as in the C2 diagram."
      ]
    }
  ]
